# Storybook Stories Rule

Components need storybook stories that demonstrate their functionality and variants.

## Story Location
- Stories should be placed in `packages/storybook/src/stories/components/{component-name}`
- The path should mirror the component's location in the core package
- For example:
  - Component: `packages/core/src/components/spectrum-button/spectrum-button.tsx`
  - Story: `packages/storybook/src/stories/components/spectrum-button/spectrum-button.stories.tsx`

## Story Requirements
- Each component should have a comprehensive story file
- Stories should demonstrate all variants, states, and use cases
- Keep stories up to date with component changes
- Use proper TypeScript types and Storybook controls
- Include examples of all component features

## Story Name
- Stories are prefixed with Spectrum, SpectrumButton as an example

## Best Practices
- Use meaningful story titles that reflect the component hierarchy
- Group related stories using the `title` property
- Provide controls for all component props
- Include documentation and usage examples
- Test all component states and variants

